1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,141
Tenant rating scores every tenant from
zero to one hundred, from how

2
00:00:04,141 --> 00:00:07,937
they have actually paid and behaved over
the last two years.

3
00:00:07,937 --> 00:00:09,662
It is a premium feature.

4
00:00:09,662 --> 00:00:12,078
Once it is switched on for your

5
00:00:12,078 --> 00:00:14,148
organisation, Tenant ratings appears under
Leasing.

6
00:00:14,148 --> 00:00:16,564
Grade A, excellent, is eighty-five and
above.

7
00:00:16,564 --> 00:00:18,634
B, good, is seventy and above.

8
00:00:18,634 --> 00:00:22,775
C, fair, is fifty and above, and D, poor,
is below fifty.

9
00:00:22,775 --> 00:00:25,536
Tenants without enough history yet are
marked New.

10
00:00:25,536 --> 00:00:28,987
Filter by grade or by property, search by
name, sort

11
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:32,093
by score, and export the list as a
spreadsheet.

12
00:00:32,093 --> 00:00:34,163
Select a grade to see why.

13
00:00:34,163 --> 00:00:35,888
Every tenant starts at seventy.

14
00:00:35,888 --> 00:00:38,304
Each event that moved the score is

15
00:00:38,304 --> 00:00:40,720
listed with its date and its points.

16
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:44,170
Fatima's cheques that cleared on time add
one point each.

17
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:47,276
Her cheque that bounced in April takes
away fifteen.

18
00:00:47,276 --> 00:00:49,002
That leaves sixty, a C.

19
00:00:49,002 --> 00:00:52,797
Late payments, penalties, write-offs and
missed meetings take points away too.

20
00:00:52,797 --> 00:00:55,558
Early renewals add them, and events more
than

21
00:00:55,558 --> 00:00:57,974
a year old count at half weight.

22
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:00,044
Rajesh has scored eighty-one, a B.

23
00:01:00,044 --> 00:01:03,150
A Company Admin can add a manual
adjustment of

24
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:06,256
up to thirty points either way, with a
reason.

25
00:01:06,256 --> 00:01:08,326
Plus five: referred a new tenant.

26
00:01:08,326 --> 00:01:10,742
Rajesh moves to eighty-six, an A, and

27
00:01:10,742 --> 00:01:12,812
the history shows who added it.

28
00:01:12,812 --> 00:01:16,263
The same grade appears in Renewal season,
on each contract,

29
00:01:16,263 --> 00:01:19,369
and on the tenant's profile, so it is in

30
00:01:19,369 --> 00:01:22,474
front of you when you decide a renewal
offer.

31
00:01:22,474 --> 00:01:24,890
Ratings are recalculated every night, and
the

32
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:27,306
details panel is always up to date.

33
00:01:27,306 --> 00:01:29,376
Tenants never see their own rating.
